, against a 2-year median of 26%. That is about one point above the median. The series rises from 24% in 2024 to 26% in 2025 and 27% in 2026.\n- **Skew:** It is flat, so downside protection isn't being priced at a premium. Nor is there a discount on upside calls.\n- **Verdict:** Vol is neither cheap nor expensive, so you get no pricing edge from buying now. The decision rests on your view of the stock, not on how the options are priced.\n\n**Risks to the underlying (from other nodes' findings, not option pricing):**\n- Utilities account for 62% of VLTX holdings' orders. Pellham Power is 35% of that and Norvane is 21%, so the order book is concentrated.\n- Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering and scaled back procurement.\n- Utility bond spreads widened 30bp to 165bp in Q3.\n- Data-centre connection growth is expected to slow to 9% in 2027.\n- Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18% and Norvane up 12%, which supports demand.\n\nConcentrated customers and tighter financing for those customers could hurt VLTX, yet IV is only slightly above its median. The market doesn't seem to be charging extra for that risk. That helps a long-vol position a little, but only if you think the risk is underpriced.\n\nIf you add this month, size it for the customer-concentration and financing risks. Before committing, check the actual premium, breakeven and expiry against your target move.","ttft_ms":2074,"type":"result","duration_ms":25414,"uuid":"326a7901-dd90-43b9-aecc-e82f2470ebef","ttft_stream_ms":1185,"time_to_request_ms":163,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":30,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":13,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":9,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":4,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":10,"client_creation":11,"re